meta {
  name: read the operator settings
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/settings/env
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  The operator settings the UI may save, and for each one whether the value came from the process environment (which the UI cannot change) or from ~/.spectro/.env. Only the writable allow-list is ever read or reported.
  
  Fence: host — Loopback fence: the TCP peer must be loopback AND the Host header must be localhost/127.0.0.1/::1. A REST client passes automatically when it targets http://localhost:<port>. A LAN IP or rebound DNS name in the URL answers a blank 404.
  
  Writes state: no
}
